# pfe-rs mapfile: EIP, Private IP, Tunnel Src, Tunnel Dst, Port
#
# --tunnel gre (recommended): Port is unused. Tunnel src = the ENI's private
#   IP (the cloud NATs it back to the EIP on egress, so the back-end GRE
#   tunnel's remote = the EIP). Tunnel dst = back-end host IP. Back-end:
#   one "ip link add pfe-greN type gre local <tunnel dst> remote <EIP>" per
#   frontend; see backend-dsr.sh.
# --tunnel fou (compat only): Port = FoU decap port. Kernel fou ipproto-4
#   will NOT deliver a bare client packet (it expects an IPIP payload and
#   needs a registered tunnel handler) -- only use fou against a back-end
#   with its own userspace decap.
203.0.113.10,10.0.0.10,10.0.0.10,198.51.100.20,5555
